[00:20.15]The world bustles, all for profit;
[00:27.97]The world clamors, all for gain.
[00:35.92]Troubled with hardship, the cold and heat of life bring no return.
[00:43.89]What joy is there in life, what sorrow in death?
[00:52.07]To push the wicked out brings resentment, so one must feign indifference and yielding.
[00:59.84]People's hearts have been vile and foul since the distant past
[01:07.97]The steps to heaven are climbed by the world,
[01:16.45]They stumble blindly on the edge of the abyss.
[01:24.19]The northern rebels left their hometowns young.
[01:31.87]The sages traveled in seclusion, roaming freely in the Eastern Mountains.
[01:39.96]Alas, their recklessness was tempered by fate.
[01:47.73]Privileged sons shall never be hanged in the streets
[01:56.14]The righteous are often from the slums,
[02:03.87]The traitors are often scholars.
[02:28.32]Lanterns illuminate for ten thousand miles; the road is long and arduous.
[02:37.53]Rain comes and goes, but cannot wash away the absurdity.
[02:47.21]Several times the fish leaped, 'til the night rattles the strings
[02:56.53]The bird of Da Peng is rising with the wind; thirty years have passed.
[03:06.68]It is difficult for children from poor families to rise to prominence in prosperous times,
[03:16.36]Even in a thriving society, there's no lack of trading parties.
[03:26.00]Born with a free soul, I ride the journey in reverse,
[03:35.12]Treading waves and soaring through clouds with nothing to regret.
[03:44.95]With my silver saddle, I swiftly follow my own nature,
[03:52.94]For the ancient white clouds, I play a melody as tribute.
